      "definition": "A DoS attack attempts to make a service unavailable by overwhelming it with requests from a single source.",
      "syntax": "Attacker \u2192 Target",
      "example": "Flooding a web server",
      "output": "Service disrupted",
      "tips": [
        "Use firewalls and rate limiting."
      ]
    },
    {
      "topic": "Distributed Denial of Service (DDoS)",
      "definition": "A DDoS attack uses many compromised devices to overwhelm a target.",
      "syntax": "Botnet \u2192 Target",
      "example": "Botnet attack on a website",
      "output": "Network overloaded",
      "tips": [
        "Use DDoS protection services."
      ]
    },
    {
      "topic": "Man-in-the-Middle (MITM)",
